cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite our paper (Cell Reports Methods, Methods Track, 2026; Zenodo DOI below) and the archive DOI of this software package."
title: "GraphSSL-MultiCancer-GFM: Graph Self-Supervised Pretraining on Multi-Cancer Molecular Networks — Task Design Principles and the Role of Protein Language Model Features"
abstract: >
  GraphSSL-MultiCancer-GFM (GFM for short) is a Cell Reports Methods (Methods Track)
  open-source reproduction package. It benchmarks five controlled evaluation protocol for
  graph self-supervised learning (Graph SSL) on 20 human cancers from TCGA,
  integrating ESM-2 protein language model embeddings as node features,
  with an FDA-level Schuirmann-1987 TOST equivalence test (Δ₀ = 0.002) for reproducibility.
type: software
